                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_g</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>14.726245,51.944535,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Krzemionki Opatowskie Flint Mine</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry <b>County/Region:</b> Swietokrzyskie <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>4</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 50.95507 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 21.49097<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Eastern_Europe/Poland/thumb/flk6113530822.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    One of the most important Neolithic flint mines of eastern Europe, including over 4000 features, including 700 shafts of 4 major types. Near the entrances to the shafts the remains of flint workshops ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=29039" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#31_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>21.49097,50.95507,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Wołowice Flint Mine</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry <b>County/Region:</b> Malopolskie <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 49.99075 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 19.71582<br />
                    Ancient Mine, Quarry or other Industry in Malopolskie. Remains of the oldest flint mine in Poland were discovered near village of Wołowice. The mine included 9 shafts and was used since 9000 BC till ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=29067" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#31_g</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>19.71582,49.99075,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Ancient Village or Settlement]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Archeological site 53</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Zachodniopomorskie <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 53.48029 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 14.41746<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Eastern_Europe/Poland/thumb/adj_DSC06427-1.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    An archeological site in Dobra, Poland discovered in 1982 and excavated 
during 1983-1984. The site contains a mesolithic settlement from the 
late Atlantic period (6500-5700 BP). Several hundred fl...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=53502" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>14.41746,53.48029,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Brody Pomorskie Neolithic Settlement</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Pomorskie <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>2</b> Condition: <b>1</b> (5 is best)   (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 53.859605 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 18.758851<br />
                    Ancient Village or Settlement in Pomorskie. Remains of an early Neolithic settlement of Linear Pottery Culture was discovered here. Not far from the settlement archaeologists located a cemetery dated ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=29208" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_g</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>18.758851,53.859605,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Góra Grodzisko Settlement</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Slaskie <b>Alt Name:</b> Cisownica - Góra Grodzisko <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>1</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 49.7065676 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 18.7596488<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Eastern_Europe/Poland/thumb/mys_cisownica3.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    An Early Iron Age (possibly Late Bronze Age) defensive settlement located on the top of Góra Grodzisko in Cisownica. It was discovered by Bogusław Chorąży and Bożena Chorąży from the Historical...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=50934" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>18.7596488,49.7065676,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Góra Ostry Settlement</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Slaskie <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>5</b>  Access: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 49.677161 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 18.750823<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Eastern_Europe/Poland/thumb/ono_goraostry5.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
